# Release signing for Pair
#
# Copy this file to `keystore.properties` and fill in the four values. That file is gitignored;
# this template is committed so the shape of it is discoverable without exposing the secrets.
#
# ## Why a keystore is needed at all
#
# Android identifies an app by its package name *and* its signing certificate. Install a build
# signed with a different certificate over an existing one and the install fails with
# INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE. The only recovery is to uninstall first, which deletes the
# app's data — the room, the display name, the avatar, the appearance settings, all of it.
#
# A release build with no signing config is signed with a throwaway debug key, and that key is
# regenerated. So consecutive release builds look like two unrelated apps to the installer, and
# every upgrade is an uninstall. Keeping one keystore, forever, is what makes "install the new
# version" mean an update.
#
# ## If you already installed a build
#
# If a build is already on a device signed with a different key, that device cannot be updated
# in place. The first release signed with the *real* key will need one uninstall on that device.
# Every build after that installs cleanly. The data lost is local only — the room itself lives in
# the Realtime Database and is reached again by signing back in with the same anonymous account,
# which is restored with the app's own data.
#
# ## Generating a keystore
#
#     keytool -genkeypair -v \
#         -keystore pair-release.jks \
#         -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 \
#         -alias pair
#
# Then copy pair-release.jks somewhere durable and **back it up**. Losing it means the next
# release cannot be signed compatibly, which brings back the uninstall problem. It is not in this
# repository and never will be.
#
# ## The values below
#
# storeFile   path to the .jks, absolute or relative to the repository root
# storePassword  the password given to keytool
# keyAlias   the alias, `pair` in the example above
# keyPassword  the key's own password
